<article class="env-definition" id="04AC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04AC">Definition <span data-tag="04AC">83.9.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme and $B$ an algebraic space over $S$. Let $j : R \to U \times _ B U$ be a pre-relation. A morphism $\phi : U \to X$ of algebraic spaces over $B$ is called a <em>good quotient</em> if </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\phi $ is invariant, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\phi $ is affine, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\phi $ is surjective, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
condition (<a href="/tag/04A7" data-tag="04A7">3</a>) holds universally, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the functions on $X$ are the $R$-invariant functions on $U$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>